Time these two sorting implementations on a list of 100,000 random integers and tell me which is faster and by how much:
```python
def bubble(a):
    a = list(a)
    for i in range(len(a)):
        for j in range(len(a) - i - 1):
            if a[j] > a[j+1]:
                a[j], a[j+1] = a[j+1], a[j]
    return a

def builtin(a):
    return sorted(a)
```

